---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Page not found — Orrin Engine"
  description="That page doesn't exist. The engine is pre-release and pages move; here's where to go instead."
>
  <div class="shell shell--narrow">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>That page doesn't exist.</h1>
      <p>
        The site changes as the engine does, so a link may have moved or been
        renamed. Here's everything there is.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="posts" aria-label="Site">
      <article class="post-row">
        <span class="post-row__date mono">01</span>
        <a href="/docs/getting-started/">
          <h2>Documentation</h2>
          <p>Build from source, run the demo, scaffold a project, write C#.</p>
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="post-row">
        <span class="post-row__date mono">02</span>
        <a href="/roadmap/">
          <h2>Roadmap</h2>
          <p>Nine phases — what has shipped and what is still open.</p>
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="post-row">
        <span class="post-row__date mono">03</span>
        <a href="/blog/">
          <h2>Development notes</h2>
          <p>Progress on the engine, and the reasoning behind the decisions.</p>
        </a>
      </article>
      <article class="post-row">
        <span class="post-row__date mono">04</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/Orrin-Team/orrin" rel="noopener">
          <h2>The repository</h2>
          <p>Source, issue tracker and milestones.</p>
        </a>
      </article>
    </nav>

    <section class="closer">
      <a class="btn btn--accent" href="/">Back to the start</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
